{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books","id":1356534,"title":"Let's Read the Aspect Books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-22T14:53:22-08:00","id":1356534,"title":"Let's Read the Aspect Books","content":"I'm going through the Aspect books again because I remember them being pretty good and am setting up a DB game, and they're good enough that I thought I'd make a thread about it! Nothing else to say let's go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Aspect Book Air</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Intro Fiction</span><br /> <br /> Awesome story, it's been one of my favourites in Exalted and re-reading it is just as good. An old weathered man is so weary of the sorry state of the world around him he retreats to a monestary to get drunk for the rest of his days. Then a mortal woman, sharp as a tack, who's been doing more than her fair share of work still awake and trying to keep things together comes for his help. I like how Arada is characterized as well, he's gruff and simple, but not dumb. In fact if he's roused to it he brings exactly the kind of social savvy that I'd expect from a Tepet or Cathak, analyzing the situation and mapping out a strategy for victory, like a battle.<br /> <br /> I like the salt god extortion as well, especially how it builds up to a bigger plan of land seizure. Arada recognizes really quickly what's happening and has had just about enough of it after a few sentences. I also really like how Autumn torments him so much, emboldened both by her anger and her husband's descriptions of an honourable general. It leaves me hopeful that general Arada can bring back his old glory and fight the good fight to stop that madness.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Introduction</span><br /> <br /> Here we get a good description for the themes of Air, learning, thought, idealism. Whether that means carving out their own place in the Realm and engineering its demise, or grabbing the society and pulling it out of the nosedive. It also has a nice big sidebar about the worship of Mela, and how that's evolved, giving Dragonblooded the right to worship her, which they do often, but not hold proper services. Interestingly, they also mention that she may come to people in visions, in the form of a white owl or a windswept grassy plain. Something about that really speaks of the Dragons being less mundane actors and more grand godlike beings that interact with the world in vague mysterious ways.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Childhood and Self</span><br /> <br /> The introduction prepares us for a series of the brutal but efficient child rearing of the Dynasty, and also for the cases where that ideal falls though.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cathak Meladus</span><br /> <br /> I think he's the guy from Scroll of Exalts who's the sorcerer-technician near Thorns? That's about all I recall.<br /> <br /> His description of his childhood overall is, by his own words, ideal. It definitely seems that way, with his family living in a villa close enough to civilization to enjoy the fruits of it while far enough away to enjoy the countryside as well. His dream of becoming an armourer being beneath him seems a bit odd, but I imagine that's because the sorcerer savants that deal with artifacts are called something else. His exaltation is great though, exalting while asleep, and then while others would be in the throes of some terrible wracking exalted puberty he calmly goes and asks the adults what he should do. I like this kid.<br /> <br /> Ah there we go, artifacters are not armourers. He paints an interesting picture of the Heptagram too, noting it's defenses and designed ruggedness against accidents. I've met a lot of engineers like him, asking what's the good of the theory without practical applications. Not so much of a bigger picture guy, but definitely still do good and impressive work. Considering his worst complaint about the school was not fitting in so well, I'd say he had it pretty good.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kasif</span><br /> <br /> Kasif I recognize, he's a stalwart monk that's zealous and caring.<br /> <br /> I like his description of a childhood in the streets, coming off of Meladus's backstory it's a shock. He's got absolutely nothing, and rather than deftly rattling off battle formations he's just looking for his next pickpocket. Surviving the harsh winters by the kindness of of a woman in the red light district of the city might have given him that little spark that he feels later on to help those less fortunate. That's a small thing among the sea of troubles he had to face though, losing friends, and eventually betrayal.<br /> <br /> Exalting with the rage of betrayal and seeing someone he loved being hurt, a much more common way to exalt I find among players. It will be interesting to see his rise out of the dregs with his exaltation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ledaal Kes</span><br /> <br /> The expert gateway player and savant.<br /> <br /> His childhoold definitely makes me think of the way Ledaal is presented in third edition. Every part of him is being tested and examined in an attempt to refine him. They didn't really treat him like a person at all, unlike Meladus. His only respite is gateway, which to him at least makes all the rules and pieces clear, and it taught him that to strive for excellence was his path to freedom. It makes sense, if you're living in an oppressive upbringing that's forcing you to excel, then when you force yourself to excel at least you're the on in control. Also a kind of nice story about how he played a game of Gateway with the Empress and her ineffability.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately his young exaltation meant that even while away from his family he kept being prodded and tested. Although his real escape is gateway tournaments where, apparently, many of the same things go on as Cynis parties. I take it to mean that there's lots of under the table dealings, drugs and sex. Through that and the Spiral Academy he did a ton of networking, apparently realizing even that young how important connections are.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Elana</span><br /> <br /> Isn't she the one who in second edition was incompetent and slept her way to the top? I forget what her writeup is like here.<br /> <br /> Starting off right away as the child with two mortal brothers, ratcheting up the pressure to exalt. Being told this by the future Elana though she says that the affections of her brothers was bad for her upbringing and made her soft? It's cute though, they helped her with her studies and swordplay as she grew up. The pressure keeps mounting as she recites the deeds of her great ancestors and feels she must live up to them. There's a pretty brutal offhand remark about her tutors being executed for not being able to teach her to sing though.<br /> <br /> Then her brothers die, ouch, and she keeps acting out until the Palace of the Tamed Storm breaks her. Then after years of abuse she breaks her instructor, who seemed at peace with the fact that either he would kill Elana, or she would kill him, and the later was a success. Which she did, of course.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Arada</span><br /> <br /> Well we get Arada's rough and tumble upbringing. In contrast to Kes he spent nights on the town with soldiers doing what soldiers on leave do. Eventually getting to the point where they were a rich kid tough gang. Then his exaltation took him like a madness, leading to a murder and straight to the Palace of the Tamed Storm to get sorted out. I like how you can see him and how he's clever though, learning that if he plays nice that actually he can get away with a lot. <br /> <br /> Also he learns about the force of presence and how strength of personality can be just as powerful as a strong body. He learns that being tough and mean doesn't mean anything, it's about responsibility and earning respect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall it's a good chapter. It sets up an oppressive childhood for some of the air aspects, but not over the top Warhammer 40k style where less than 10% of Dynasts survive to adulthood or something silly. There are a few things that are always consistent though, if you're a Dynast much is expected of you, you will be given every opportunity to excel, and you will take them whether you like it or not. The phrase &quot;What Fire has Wrought&quot; really makes sense here, whatever you are coming out of the other side, it was forged.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next up we see their life of obligations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T16:23:05-08:00","id":1356547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books#post1356534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Elana</span><br /> <br /> Isn't she the one who in second edition was incompetent and slept her way to the top? I forget what her writeup is like here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of Lisara. Elana was in the opening comic of MoEP: Dragon-Blooded as an example of a dedicated, true to their beliefs Dynast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T17:09:05-08:00","id":1356555,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">A Life of Obligation</span><br /> <br /> Starting things right off by saying that Dynasts do not rest on their laurels or degenerate into decadence and self praise, rather they think of their power as a burden.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cathak Meladus</span><br /> <br /> So he had to convince people to let him go to Thorns, eh? So he's not totally free. Here he becomes disillusioned with the Realm, seeing the ugly side of mismanagement. Then the Mask and the Juggernaut came and smashed through their forces there, driving them back. Interestingly though, he doesn't despair, which I guess is what a Melaist would do. He points out all the places that the Realm is falling apart, and then decides that he's going to fix them, and also noting that he's not the only one who feels that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kasif</span><br /> <br /> Starting out with a pretty rough go of it, he's having all connections to his previous life severed by the Immaculate Order. For the first time ever he's got stability in his world. An outcaste, from the Realm, but still almost totally uneducated. He was drilled very hard though, apparently because if he couldn't pass and become a monk he was going to be killed, which is brutal. I'm getting a kind of jedi padawan feeling here, because after passing and becoming a full monk the one sponsoring and guiding him, Preda, still stays with him and instructs him.<br /> <br /> Then after that he's set loose, in a way, slowly. Still being watched, but now trusted to go out in the world and be a monk. He then talks about what a joy it is to be out ministering to people on the Blessed Isle. There's a bit of a hint of the duality of the order here though, keeping peasants happy where they are, and destroying a local inn for it's heretical iconography. We get a hint that even after all this time, he's not over his childhood love though. Especially after his circuit is done and he's kept in the Imperial City for a year, where he grew up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ledaal Kes</span><br /> <br /> Kes is growing a lot here, seeing how the world works first as a game, and then with more nuance. He's putting his great intelligence to good work though, as an investigator of white collar crime primarily. It's a pretty thankless job considering how unsexy it is compared to chasing down violent criminals, but it makes a big impact. Gateway tournaments again help here. Then comes the All-Seeing Eye, which in this description come across as being actually pretty scary. Undergoing a panic attack and basically making plans for his own death. Even with all his skill, knowledge and power he doesn't even think to run. When the Eye wants you dead, you're going to die, best take it with some dignity. It's a bit different from other characterizations I've seen of the Eye, it gives a good sense of how powerful they are and how powerful their reputation is.<br /> <br /> He also takes religious philosophy into his work, applying it to his accounting and investigations. He too sees many of the ills of the empire, and is striving to fix them. Also the writing is really good, his voice is totally different from, say, Arada's. He also isn't too thrilled about Melaists being too focused on martial prowess. It reminds me of that one Klingon lawyer from Star Trek who scoffed at the idea that his entire race were warriors, and how honour used to be found in the laboratory and courtroom as well as the battlefield.<br /> <br /> He's got an interesting relationship with his wife too. He loves her, and apparently they sometimes use sorcery to have sex in the way that they find most pleasing, but they also find satisfaction outside their marriage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Elana</span><br /> <br /> Okay this is bugging me, she CAN'T be the incompetent Tepet I'm thinking of...and no she's not, that's Lisara. Okay, Elana is the one from the DB chapter comic in the MoEP.<br /> <br /> She's had a rough life in the Vermillion legion though. She repeats how much she values mortal lives though, having a soft spot for him due to her brothers. Her early life seems to be defined by that moment when she defied orders and lead her dragon of soldiers in a rear guard action defending the wounded who could not retreat with the rest of the legion. Then after being sicked by that she returns home and we have a bit of a mistake with her family marrying her off, because that's not how the Dynasty works.<br /> <br /> Thankfully she doesn't focus much on that because she's been named a magistrate. Interestingly the Empress liked that she disobeyed orders and did what she thought was right, showing courage and valor, or so she said. Likely also a bit of a troublemaker for the legions, although she'd quit by then. She enjoys the freedom of being a magistate however. She then goes on to talk about hunting anathema and how she likes the simplicity of it. No negotiation, no grey area, just exhilarating combat.<br /> <br /> A nice stop on her religious life as well, and about how she questions the faith, but not really heretically? If that makes any sense. It sounds like something that she might actually bring up in a religious debate with somebody who isn't Peleps Deled and have a good discussion. Oh and now she's got the hots for one of her archons, classic. Sadly being mortal she's trapped, because she knows no matter what her best case is to watch him wither away as he ages.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Arada</span><br /> <br /> Confirming what I've been thinking about his characterization, he can turn on the charm and socialite thing when he wants to, he just doesn't want to. Poor Arada, being dragged into politics again when he hates it so much. In fact that's how he came into possession of his heirloom blade, the blade of Tepet himself apparently. Jesus, and then he just took some years off to go live up north and trade furs? Damn, that's a Power move.<br /> <br /> Then came the famous campaign against Jochim, who definitely had tiger warriors. Then the surprising final battle, Arada himself took a small force of elite soldiers, infiltrated Jochim's last fortress, killed him and burned it to the ground. A sharp contrast to the last campaign he waged, which was mismanaged and lazy to the point that it drove Arada into solitude again. He's kind of given up hope, but he does hope that the Dragons still watch over the Realm, because they really need it right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Great chapter, you really get a feel for the characters growing into their power and place in the world. A good path to how they've found their footing. It does a good job at showing the way a myriad of characters might integrate themselves into the Empire. Next we're going to learn about the world they rule from those positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T18:31:12-08:00","id":1356565,"title":"","content":"The World We Rule<br /> <br /> We first get a paragraph about how Air savants are planners of entire cultures and possibly closest of all aspects to governors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cathak Meladus</span><br /> <br /> Meladus is PISSED that the Realm has descended into infighting and selfishness. There's a bit of a creepy note in that he believes the Realm is the way to bring enlightenment and civilization to the world, probably through conquest. He's trying to work out a way to fix the Realm, but he's finding it really hard because house Cathak itself is caught up in all of this, so he can't even rely on his family to help him. He knows others feel the same, but speaking openly is dangerous. Not that he'd be killed or anything, just that he knows the best way to win is to make sure that the people tearing the Realm up don't even known he's fighting them.<br /> <br /> He's also concerned about the anathema, and thinks more should be done to stop them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kasif</span><br /> <br /> He's also mad about the Realm, but he's more angry about the poverty that he sees, and especially the disparity of wealthy and poor. People living comfortable lives in gilded halls, commanding armies while others suffer terribly. Along those same lines he laments that the Exalted forget that mortals are an equally important part of the perfected hierarchy, and would be wise to treat dynastic children as mortals, just as a reminder. Kasif might help you start an occupy Wallstreet movement it looks like. Just don't bring iconography because he will annihilate it.<br /> <br /> He also thinks that the Order is being insulated from their failure to help the peasants. Ah, well now I was more right than I thought with occupy Wallstreet, he's thinking about staging a demonstration in the Imperial City. He has a darker side too though. The heresy of the Antitheses, basically the IO's four horsemen of the apocalypse, is something that really gets under his skin and I'm pretty sure he would react violently to it, considering he helped bring the executioners to a village to execute them for idolatry.<br /> <br /> Coming back around to his light side, he's not a fan of the way young mortal Dynasts are treated. There's too much pressure put on them, and at the same time given so much that they never learn to appreciate. Again he's thinking about another demonstration to show displeasure about the Realm's infighting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ledaal Kes</span><br /> <br /> In theme here, Kes is mad at the Empire for allowing a patriot like Nezzegar to be punished and forcing him to work in the shadows when he's one of the people actually working to keep it together. Kes is pretty open in his thoughts about the Sidereals as well, working with them and house Iselsi. As a bonus he's working with the Imperial Treasury to keep some kind of non-partisan features of the imperial government together. In a unique position as a treasury official and All-Seeing-Eye agent he's got a seriously wide view of the Empire, taking in the really big pictures.<br /> <br /> Kes has also got his mind on mortals, not surprising considering he works in the treasury which is full of patricians. He recognizes well that mortals are the foundation of the empire, and how incredibly stupid it is to forget that. He also mentions something about the new aristocracy of the Underworld, meaning the Abyssal exalted. He doesn't find them to be a concern compared to the infighting of the Realm, but he's not foolish. He knows they're dangerous, he just knows that if they don't unite they won't have to be dangerous to destroy them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Elana</span><br /> <br /> I won't retread anything except to say she's unhappy with House infighting. She's also unhappy with the infighting within her own house too though. Its own little civil war among different bloodlines. She's got allies who think as she does, but they're young and at the moment lack respect *cough* PCs *cough*. Elana also really likes mortals, almost to the point of revering them. Just as long as they don't do something silly like try to end imperial rule of their satrapy.<br /> <br /> Really nicely though her mortal archon is a major part of her life, and a pillar that holds her up when she's weak. I think PCs could stand to have a few mortals like that around, although it's a bit easier with DBs because they're usually not charging alone into utterly impossible odds. Not frequently anyway. Speaking of her opinions on Solars are a lot more in line with what I was thinking the standard Dynast idea would be. They're terrible, frightening, and coming to tear down the Realm, and the only way to stop them is to cut them off early.<br /> <br /> In her opinion the legions have also fallen, as much as the great houses. The pampered political appointees in the officer corps are dragging down their might.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tepet Arada</span><br /> <br /> Arada is done with the Realm as a whole, all the ideas of it that are crumbling around, he's just sick of it. I think he just plans on living out the rest of his days trying to do the right thing in the moment and forget all that other stuff. Especially since he openly admits here that the Tepet legions were driven up to fight the Bull to die because they were the strongest house at the time.<br /> <br /> I like Arada. When he's talking about respect he recognizes the difference between forcing mortals to jump through ridiculous hoops just to talk to you, and mortals who's respect you've earned properly. While he'd agree with Kasif on that front, he'd disagree a lot about Anathema. He's seen anathema scared of their own power, and of him, ones who didn't even want to be anathema.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall another good one. We're learning about everyone's position, there's a lot of hooks for adventures in there. The last thing Kes needs right now is for Kasif to start some shit demanding that the empire needs to divert funds to help the poor, when he's barely keeping the imperial funds from being completely emptied into the purses of the great houses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think I'm done for tonight, Voices Not Our Own will have to wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T10:10:06-08:00","id":1356660,"title":"","content":"Eagerly awaiting your thoughts on AB: Earth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T15:52:44-08:00","id":1356710,"title":"","content":"Voices not Our Own is really meaty, because now we get to see what everyone else thinks about our POV characters. There's so many people here that I might not be able to touch on everyone. That's okay though, you should read it yourself if you're interested.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mortals</span><br /> <br /> First we start off with mortals, who make up the vast majority of the Realm and many important interactions with Dynasts. Primarily those interactions are dominated by the Immaculate Faith. Their whole culture is steeped in it, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Starting off with Opal Mountain, a friend to Meladus and an armourer. The paragraph talks about cobbling together a suit of ancient dragon armor for Meladus to return to full function. Dragon Armor is actually something mentioned in the Dragonblooded illumination in the corebook. I'm not sure how it's going to translate into 3e, if it ever even gets stats. Third edition has moved a bit away from the magitech side of Exalted, but the power armor was also a pretty cool addition to the game. Just as long as it isn't just like regular armor except way better I think it would do fine.<br /> <br /> Then we get to Pug, the innkeeper for the inn that Kasif singlehandedly wrecked. We find out that his life is pretty well broken, and tells us that everyone who went to worship the local god at the shrine was executed for heresy. Kasif is uncompromising when it comes to willful heresy. If you know the faith, and know what you're doing is against the faith, and aren't being forced into it, there's no excuse. That alone would make him really hard to work with for a lot of players, whatever else he is he's a zealot.<br /> <br /> The next mortal also comments on that zeal, which makes a lot of sense. The order took him out of poverty, gave his life structure and meaning, and taught him to strive for something, and now he's taking that grit and determination from the streets and backing it with faith and exalted might.<br /> <br /> Moving on to Beren now, Tepet Elana's special archon friend. It's interesting to see a mortal working so closely with an exalt, sharing the dangers and confiding in eachother. I guess magistrates enjoy less separation from mortals than other Dynasts, along with those in the military. Or maybe there's just less separation than I imagined anyway.<br /> <br /> Autumn Bloom talking about Arada is one of my favourites here. She doesn't just stand up to him as a gag, like &quot;Womp womp, she's not kowtowing like your average peasant.&quot; She actually respects Arada a damn bit more than other Dyansts she knows of. In fact she's very empathetic towards him, is trying to help guide him to do the right thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dragonblooded</span><br /> <br /> Here, must like with Kasif, we also see a chink in Meladus's armor. He was a brave, dedicated, and very morally guided soul, but his sister sees his naive nature being his downfall. A moral compass can tell you where to go, but can't guide you around all the pitfalls along the way. She just hopes failure doesn't break him. Considering she dies shortly after this and he keeps going it looks like it hasn't. The text doesn't seem to judge one way or the other either. Is Meladus a fool for striving to save the Empire from disaster? Or is his sister a fool for giving up and wanting to leave. Who knows?<br /> <br /> We also get another hint of the warrior culture taking over a bit too much when one of his instructors at the Heptagram laments all this study and focus of a brilliant mind and only seeing the application in war.<br /> <br /> We also get something from the monk who's training Kasif. It turns out he's not happy about the tradition to kill prospective monks if they fail their test so early. Noting that he himself almost failed, and Kasif is really trying very hard, with the least ideal upbringing imaginable. The Immaculate Order really needs somebody to step in here, stand up and make the process maybe just a bit more lenient.<br /> <br /> Bal Keraz gives us another jolt of just how scary the All Seeing Eye can be. As the head of the Imperial Treasury you'd think the Eye wouldn't cause that much uneasiness, but it does. Kes is actually shaping up to be pretty cool. He's kind of like a superhero accountant, except according to his wife he's working himself to death. Hopefully her determination to get her husband back can help him to figure out some kind of balance where the treasury doesn't fall apart.<br /> <br /> Later on we get a one-two punch of the duties of at Dynast, with Tepet Elana being fussed over by her relatives and prospective husband. Both of whom are conspiring to tear away the shield of her magistracy and force her to marry somebody. It gives me a mind to include that in a game as something that could be sprung as a sudden game-changer. Out of nowhere family members practically dragging you to a ceremony to be wed.<br /> <br /> I like the Roseblack's description of Arada as well. Seeing his more personal and vulnerable side, not just the invincible general who could lead men into the maw of Hell and back again. At the same time shes chastising him secretly for giving up. She should meet Autumn and see how she's leading Arada back into the fight.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirits</span><br /> <br /> The salt god that was part of that conspiracy at the beginning is here too. Even the least gods are sensing the change of the Time of Tumult and looking to take a piece for themselves. Specifically by tearing down the stability of the Empire and forcing their strength on their domains. It's a little thing that shows how under the noses of the powerful waging war, the influence it has when they turn against themselves. All the things that were being pressed down by their might are now rising up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next is a chapter with records from the Low First Age of the Shogunate. There are many entries here too, so I might skip a few. I'll pick out the important ones that I think should be commented on. After that the charms section is almost useless now, but some of the enchanted items might be worth a look like the aformentioned Dragon Armor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T17:05:43-08:00","id":1356955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1356555#post1356555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">A Life of Obligation</span><br /> <br /> and we have a bit of a mistake with her family marrying her off, because that's not how the Dynasty works.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it is not. Older editions were more 'oh the Realm is totally matriarchal' but then portray it as a pretty standard patriarchal society with more opportunity for women than history had. But it is what it is, most of these books have some cruft that doesn't fit in 3e quite right anymore but a lot of cool stuff as well.<br /> <br /> The Outcaste airship pirate in Water is one of my favorite stories, since for a while I had struggled hard with getting a good handle DB outcaste stories that aren't just 'like a Solar but can't kill as big of things quickly', but hers feels very DB in its way. That and the nice selection of stuff consolidated in WFHW which I'm sure is a lot less new than my brain tells me it, but aside from the Forest Witches and Lookshy I'm not sure I recognize any of them.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you're doing this though because hell yes hype the Aspect books. They're <i>so </i>good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T18:53:37-08:00","id":1356968,"title":"","content":"I'll probably have a lot to say on Mnemon when we get there. Nice work so far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T11:07:21-08:00","id":1357071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1356955#post1356955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That it is not. Older editions were more 'oh the Realm is totally matriarchal' but then portray it as a pretty standard patriarchal society with more opportunity for women than history had. But it is what it is, most of these books have some cruft that doesn't fit in 3e quite right anymore but a lot of cool stuff as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe The Dragon-Blooded uses the word &quot;Martiachal&quot; ever. The Heads of Households are presented in gender neutral terms. Several insitutions are referred to as meritocracies. There's clear sex discrimination against women who bear children out of wedlock.<br /> <br /> It's matrilinial. Children belong to their mother's house and social class. It's ruled by an Empress.<br /> <br /> But it's not, and not presented as, matriarchal.<br /> <br /> A Tepet being married off to house Peleps to secure an alliance is completely in-genre. And that's how it works: the children will be Tepets, but the husbands didn't join the wife's house until 3E (The Dragon-Blooded has a neat sidebar on this on page 114). Do note that Elena is not expected to work for Kerel's house because of gender -- it's because of the political balance between the houses. And I imagine Votival is Kerel's mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-26-2019, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T13:15:27-08:00","id":1357091,"title":"","content":"Man, I can't stand Kasif. Compared to 3e's take on the IO, what he did to those villagers was excessive and cruel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:15:18-08:00","id":1357104,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Records from the Before</span></u><br /> <br /> <br /> We start out with a little paragraph about how the Dragonblooded of the Realm view the Shogunate to be a shining golden era of grand culture, now lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Religious Tracts</span><br /> <br /> The <i>Hesiesh Youth Fiery Murder Society. </i>I mean, that says it all right there pretty much. A religious order obsessed with martyring themselves and killing anathema.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shogun Assassinated!</span><br /> <br /> The start of what I think will be a theme with these records, the Shogunate's greatest problems came from their infighting. The current Shogun was seen as soft, wanting to keep an open dialogue with rebels and barbarians, and for that he was assassinated. Of course the not-very-subtle subtext is that this was also a power grab by the crown prince. Tearing parts of the Shogunate up if it means he's in power now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Purloined Letter</span><br /> <br /> A Sidereal letter to Chejop Kejak that indeed keeps with the themes of factional infighting, and how had it is to plan for. If they thought the Shogunate was a nightmare to wrangle the Second Age must seem impossible. Especially since there's a hint of lamentation that this fallen world lacks the horrors of the High First Age, but it also means they actually have to work to keep it going.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Northern Dragon Fund Collapses</span><br /> <br /> Here we see the Shogunate's response to a failing but critical business, government custodianship. There's just a hint of something shadier going on under the surface though, maybe it's nothing. The firm is supposedly going to be returned to the family who ruined it in the first place after the government gets it back on its feet, to me that's a bit suspect. Immediately after we get a warning that this is not to leak out into the general population, as faith in the Shogunate financial systems is a pillar of the economy that can not stand to be eroded.<br /> <br /> I wonder if a similar story could be run with the Imperial Treasury?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fair Folk Attack the South</span><br /> <br /> The first headline about horrors from beyond the Shogunate, and it's a spit take inducing one million hobgoblin assault. Except it's actually just more internal struggles, really. The water starved lower classes aided the Fey in their invasion and the Shogunate is enacting the simple response of deploying soldiers and enforcing military sweeps of civilian areas. At this point they don't really have a choice, the rabble are summoning faerie monsters into the world but you'd think paying some more attention to the low class mortal population would have been able to stop this prematurely.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Hand off Mela Smites the Land</span><br /> <br /> Well this is an epic, if embellished, account of one of the greatest conflicts during the Usurpation. A battle of around eight high essence Solars/Lunars, their titanic skyship, and a few hundred terrestrials with over a dozen warstriders, Thousand Forged Dragons. It all ends with a fantasy version of a nuclear explosion, complete with radioactive fallout sickening dragonblooded and slaying mortals. The interesting thing here is that it talks about a point in the Usurpation that wasn't just an assassination attempt, this was a massive pitched battle. It also talks about Lunars fighting alongside Solars in their last stand.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Of Eyem, Eternally Preserved Lord and Savant of the Dragonblooded-Shogunate</span><br /> <br /> Wow, this is an interesting one. A kind of sci-fi concept of the thinking machine IAM attempting to take over the Shogunate, and eventually the Realm, and being defeated each time. I'm kind of curious though, here even the learned savant says that IAM was created not by the Anathema, but by the Dragonblooded. I didn't think that was true? Or was it changed in 2e? Either way, it's cool that they reference many more thinking machines stored in the Heptagram, and talk of how to safely interact with them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">From the Journals of Marsan Lan</span><br /> <br /> And this is an exploration of more fucked up Creation science gone crazy, it's also really cool. Basically, from what I gather, they're making the matrix, except 100% of the computing power is coming from mortal minds. Of course, since this is Creation and not Earth, they're not making a digital world, but a massive shared dream to run simulations and try to advance medicine. The art goes well along with this, a genius pushed too far in some darkened lab trying to produce something grand and terrible in secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:32:05-08:00","id":1357111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357104#post1357104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Records from the Before</span></u><br /> <br /> <br /> We start out with a little paragraph about how the Dragonblooded of the Realm view the Shogunate to be a shining golden era of grand culture, now lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Religious Tracts</span><br /> <br /> The <i>Hesiesh Youth Fiery Murder Society. </i>I mean, that says it all right there pretty much. A religious order obsessed with martyring themselves and killing anathema.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shogun Assassinated!</span><br /> <br /> The start of what I think will be a theme with these records, the Shogunate's greatest problems came from their infighting. The current Shogun was seen as soft, wanting to keep an open dialogue with rebels and barbarians, and for that he was assassinated. Of course the not-very-subtle subtext is that this was also a power grab by the crown prince. Tearing parts of the Shogunate up if it means he's in power now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Purloined Letter</span><br /> <br /> A Sidereal letter to Chejop Kejak that indeed keeps with the themes of factional infighting, and how had it is to plan for. If they thought the Shogunate was a nightmare to wrangle the Second Age must seem impossible. Especially since there's a hint of lamentation that this fallen world lacks the horrors of the High First Age, but it also means they actually have to work to keep it going.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Northern Dragon Fund Collapses</span><br /> <br /> Here we see the Shogunate's response to a failing but critical business, government custodianship. There's just a hint of something shadier going on under the surface though, maybe it's nothing. The firm is supposedly going to be returned to the family who ruined it in the first place after the government gets it back on its feet, to me that's a bit suspect. Immediately after we get a warning that this is not to leak out into the general population, as faith in the Shogunate financial systems is a pillar of the economy that can not stand to be eroded.<br /> <br /> I wonder if a similar story could be run with the Imperial Treasury?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fair Folk Attack the South</span><br /> <br /> The first headline about horrors from beyond the Shogunate, and it's a spit take inducing one million hobgoblin assault. Except it's actually just more internal struggles, really. The water starved lower classes aided the Fey in their invasion and the Shogunate is enacting the simple response of deploying soldiers and enforcing military sweeps of civilian areas. At this point they don't really have a choice, the rabble are summoning faerie monsters into the world but you'd think paying some more attention to the low class mortal population would have been able to stop this prematurely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really changes how the Fair Folk invasion feels. Not badly, either, since it might be able to write the Deathlords out of trying to offer up Creation, which they probably wouldn't have been able to do since they didn't actually exist in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Hand off Mela Smites the Land</span><br /> <br /> Well this is an epic, if embellished, account of one of the greatest conflicts during the Usurpation. A battle of around eight high essence Solars/Lunars, their titanic skyship, and a few hundred terrestrials with over a dozen warstriders, Thousand Forged Dragons. It all ends with a fantasy version of a nuclear explosion, complete with radioactive fallout sickening dragonblooded and slaying mortals. The interesting thing here is that it talks about a point in the Usurpation that wasn't just an assassination attempt, this was a massive pitched battle. It also talks about Lunars fighting alongside Solars in their last stand.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Of Eyem, Eternally Preserved Lord and Savant of the Dragonblooded-Shogunate</span><br /> <br /> Wow, this is an interesting one. A kind of sci-fi concept of the thinking machine IAM attempting to take over the Shogunate, and eventually the Realm, and being defeated each time. I'm kind of curious though, here even the learned savant says that IAM was created not by the Anathema, but by the Dragonblooded. I didn't think that was true? Or was it changed in 2e? Either way, it's cool that they reference many more thinking machines stored in the Heptagram, and talk of how to safely interact with them. </div> </div> </div>I think the implication in DotFA was that a mostly blasted-out collection of IAM bits was used as a model for Eyem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">From the Journals of Marsan Lan</span><br /> <br /> And this is an exploration of more fucked up Creation science gone crazy, it's also really cool. Basically, from what I gather, they're making the matrix, except 100% of the computing power is coming from mortal minds. </div> </div> </div>That actually makes it much closer to the original script of The Matrix, where the network of minds held everyone into a shared, prison-like dream world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T15:30:25-08:00","id":1357122,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Miracles of Mela</span></u><br /> <br /> I'll skip the charms chapter, basically there's a few charms that show up first here that become signature DB abilities later on. There are some interesting artifacts though. For one the Fivefold Harmonic Resonator makes an appearance, which basically acts as an adapter, letting you attune to any magical material. Could something like this exist in 3e, letting you become resonant with artifacts that you aren't normally? Maybe, but the cost would have to be pretty high.<br /> <br /> We also get a Mundane Box, which is a box that's plain to the point of increasing the difficulty of finding objects in the box to +2 and even automattically defeating All-Encompassing Sorcerer Sight.<br /> <br /> There's also a slew of artifacts with interesting properties, reducing the weight of an object, controlling wind and storms, using wind to substitute for construction labor, and even Icemind itself. Another artificial mind that we have some nice stats for. All of it generates the imagery of a pretty wondrous world. A construction site with 1000 pound blocks of stone being wheeled in, lightened by Windslave Disks, the weather being kept pleasant and breezy by a Sky Mantis Tower and half the work being performed by the wind itself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Military</span><br /> <br /> After that though, we get to the military section. I remember Elemental Lenses well from 2e. It's definitely more complex in this book though, but I think it might work as an item that has evocations in 3e?<br /> <br /> Now we get to the serious meat though, Most Terrifying Armor of the Air Dragon. Armor that increases the strength and resistance of the wearer, with a helmet that allows them to see in the dark and sharpens their senses. It can cloak itself in shadows and even helps avoid detection by divination magic, with gauntlets that channel lightning into a weapon. Finally it can be made to fly, either temporarily in combat, or permanently at 60 miles per hour outside of it. It's a truly epic piece of artiface, and I really hope to see something like this in 3e.<br /> <br /> I can only imagine that to balance it out it would need like a 15 mote attunement cost, be artifact 5, and keep some of the hearthstone and maintenance requirements, and some of the effects may have to be evocations.<br /> <br /> Also something that I'd forgotten about, the Reaver Dragonfly. An enormous mechanical insect assassin that acts kind of as the fantasy equivalent of a combat drone. That'd be a nice little addition to a Dragonblooded Hunter. Plus you get the image of the imperious lord who doesn't want to messy her hands with hunting some quarry through the slums so she sends her little toy to go do the work while she sits on her horse outisde.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Signature Characters</span></u><br /> <br /> Here we see a bunch of characters, both as prospective PCs and NPCs. I'll skip a lot of the stuff that would just be retreading.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Meladus</span><br /> <br /> He's got an interesting habit of channeling electricity between his hands. Little things like that are, I think, technically not possible without spending motes? Although I'm not sure in a game if I wouldn't allow it anyway as part of a stunt. He's also built in a way that I very rarely see, even though I think it's probably closer to design intentions. He doesn't have a single 5 in any ability, but what he has does look pretty fun<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kasif</span><br /> <br /> Equipped with some very basic immaculate martial arts he's a fairly solid fighter. I was surprised to see him favour Larceny at first but then I remembered he grew up a pickpocket. His abilities are spread super thin though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Other Notable Air Aspects</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nellens Poramo</span><br /> <br /> My boy Nellens Poramo! Look at him. He's so handsome. Confidant little half smile, immaculately dressed with his cloak there, bearing the brunt of an older generation mocking his idealism completely unperturbed. He's just great. One just has to overlook the fact that after he heals the Scarlett Dynasty his plan is to reassert full control over the Threshold. Also his writeup mentions something that I think is a great plot point for a lot of games, with the Empress gone perhaps the Deliberative will become the new power in the Realm. Rather than an empire with a monarch they might have some kind of reform into a collaborative government.<br /> <br /> The only thing with Poramo is, he needs help. He has almost no allies to speak of at the moment. Enter the PCs...<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ragara Szaya</span><br /> <br /> Kes's wife, here's she's depicted as basically a noble adventurer from DnD. She's a merchant-warrior-explorer ranging far afield in the Threshold diving in to first age tombs and plundering them for artiface and knowledge. In fact she has contacts in the Threshold all over the world, and is equipped with an arsenal of sorcery and artifacts. She'd make a really good benefactor for a young group of PCs that are playing a more DnD style game. Either in her company or being sent out by her to places she no longer has the time to go to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Peleps Cordera</span><br /> <br /> Now here's an interesting one. She's one of the Realms greatest poets...at least supposedly. Every work attributed to her is one she's never seen before in her life, and yet somebody with a lot of power is setting her up to be this great artist. I like the panic in the Peleps admiralty who understand right away that this can only be bad news. Nobody is propping up one of their scions to be a heart wrenching powerful writer without either wanting something in return, or making some kind of embarrassing reversal. They're not simultaneously launching an investigation and teaching her to be a great poet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Iselsi Jolin</span><br /> <br /> Otherwise known as Death Blossom, the terror of the Realm. Striking out from her <i>secret volcano lair </i>to try and dismantle the Realm one assassination at a time. She's not really a Dynast though, she serves a shard of House Iselsi that just wants to make people lose faith in the system and have it fall apart into chaos. The disappearance of the Empress must be like a godsend to her and her ilk. Somebody should either stop her to save the Realm, or join her to tear it down.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Windtamer Cynis Mond</span><br /> <br /> Finally, we get to the end. Mond is a great man, a powerful sorcerer, and a visionary for his time. He created entirely new terrestrial charms, patterns for sails, kites, wind artifacts, and geomantic patterns. He doesn't even touch the ground anymore, instead in a state of perpetual fight. A good character to have around as an extremely powerful, if eccentric, old wizard. I get the feeling from him that talking to him for five minutes would seem to yield nothing, but over days of letting those words linger in your head you'd see some kind of deep and high level wisdom in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> AAANNND that's it for Aspect Book: Air! I think a pretty good start. Very good, extremely well written, and nice in the focuses that it takes. I'm really looking forward to that continuing in Earth, up next!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T16:34:47-08:00","id":1357127,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Nellens Poramo being decieved by Manosque Cyan back in 2e? Sounds like PCs need to save him from a false friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T16:38:54-08:00","id":1357128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357127#post1357127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Nellens Poramo being decieved by Manosque Cyan back in 2e? Sounds like PCs need to save him from a false friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but that's 2e, and I think part of the non-canon Return of the Scarlett Empress anyway. Although I could definitely see using that in a game that had Poramo in it. The PCs come back from some far off adventure to find that Poramo has found another new ally to join the PCs in their cause, except there's just something not right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T17:03:03-08:00","id":1357132,"title":"","content":"It's interesting that Meladus doesn't have any 5s, because that probably wouldn't fly in 3e if he wanted to keep his central concept of working with First Age Artifice, which is a major bonus point hog for needing 5s in Lore, Occult, and Craft (Artifact), which in turn practically requires another Craft Ability at 5. And, of course, sorcery.<br /> <br /> I'm also kind of cursing the book for the presence of the Fivefold Harmonic Adapter, which was way too cheap even back in the day; ideally, thanks to the broken effect of MM bonuses from the beginning, it would have been expensive and higher-level from the starting line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T22:04:52-08:00","id":1357168,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:36px\"><u>Aspect Book: Earth</u></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Introduction Fiction</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">We start off this book with a fiction about Mnemon herself. I remember this one pretty well, but it's still a bit odd reading about Mnemon and how dirty she's getting here. Going herself down to the docks in her enchanted cloak to treat with an anathema messenger of the Mask of Winters. They do a good job of showing her power though, utilizing demons to aid her information gathering, artifacts to help espionage, and powerful charms in her sparring. She's also devout, despising the anathema that she must work with, but her ambition outweighs that devotion, for now.<br /> <br /> I also like how she's dealing with the Mask. She wants the Blessed Isle, he wants the Scavenger Lands, let's make some magic happen. Both in full knowledge of course that once they get what they want, the Mask will want the Isle and she will want the Scavenger Lands. I really appreciate her bluntness here too. She's not stupid, but she's also got no time for pleasantries or diplomacy when dealing with these monsters. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Introduction</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Different from the idealistic aspects of Air, the Earth aspects hold structure and order above all else. They're meditative, enduring, and impossible to shake from a task that they set themselves on. Rocky would like them, it's not about how hard you hit, it's about how hard you can get hit and keep going. Sadly I can't comment on the literary resources as I haven't myself read any of them. I appreciate the idea of Earth aspects being the embodiment of Bushido, however. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Childhood and Self</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cynis Takgana</span><br /> <br /> Takgana is starting off this story in a bad way. He's talking about a wonderful life in the south-east, with beautiful vineyards, a prospective love that he will marry, and a mother who's guiding him towards taking over the business. Yeah, and here we go, his jealous mortal sister slices his testicles from him, just as he exalts. Then his whole life falls apart, his doting mother won't even look at him, he's going to become a monk and spend the next few years of his life confused and hollow. At this point it's almost a blessing that the Cloister works him so hard.<br /> <br /> Afterwards his life as a eunuch is pretty rough, although the order looks to be pretty accommodating, offering to train him in martial arts styles that fit a low amounts of masculine essence. We also get some good worldbuilding with the Iron Horses, immaculate prospectives from the Cloister who bond with eachother in the face of impossible challenges.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crow</span><br /> <br /> Another outcaste from within the Realm! I have no idea why, maybe just from PCs, but almost every outcaste I imagine comes from outside the Realm proper. Her interaction with a pair of Dynasts is pretty good though. On receiving a complement she drops down and swears fealty, and then bemusedly the Dynast buys out her entire stall of apples. I like the touch that she seemed to have an okay life, and wanted to take some of it with her as a token into the Dynasty, but then left it as she thought it wasn't proper for a dragonblooded warrior to carry around a scrap of her security blanket.<br /> <br /> Then when she gets to secondary school she makes some fast friends with other outcastes. One of whom doesn't follow the other two into the legions, which I feel will come up later. The one who does though gets his larynx crushed and becomes mute for life after a brutal assault from older students. Pasaip's Stair gives no fucks about student safety, especially since years later she gets her revenge by sneak attacking the two with a knife and killing one. What a waste, although it seems like the legions didn't exactly lose two of their better commanders in that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ragara Jasir</span><br /> <br /> Kept prim and proper by his family growing up he's getting a lot more regimented an upbringing than most. Jesus and his brother tried to have him killed? Aspect Book: Earth is shaping up to have way more violent childhoods than Air. We get some more about familial politics, and then a deep religious experience of exaltation, feeling the whole world around him, and feeling linked to his brother, who probably exalted around the same time.<br /> <br /> We get another little jab of family control here as well, just like Takgana. He wanted to go to the Cloister but his father ruled that he would go to the Spiral Academy instead, and that is that. It's also giving me a bit of anxiety when it talks about the accounting courses. I've had to take a few in University before and they're so mind numbingly, wretchedly boring. <i>The Complete and Annotated Directory of Range and Departments within the Thousand Scales of the Dragon 8th Edition</i> sounds like exactly the kind of book that would send me to sleep in minutes. He also learns about the power of money-lending and how people with little financial liberty can be taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> He then takes the knowledge and uses the leverage of his coin to go searching through the work that the academy does for even more important information. God I am really not liking the skeevy nature of Jasir here. It makes me want to join the Imperial Treasury and bring the hammer down on what I imagine will be his white collar crimes in the future. I'm going to come busting into his house with a bunch of Black Helms and seize is fucking dirty-ass ledgers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moias</span><br /> <br /> Oof, well at least this isn't a violent childhood. Just one with a mother who is distant and abusive to her father, who is himself dull and controlling. At least her biological father helped her out with a good strong education. More argument and disagreement over secondary school, until eventually she heads for the House of Bells. At which she hunts captured Fey that have been brought to the school and set loose in the hunting grounds. Afterwards one of the more noble looking fairfolk was taken away, having earned his freedom through avoiding the student hunters with a look that all had gone according to plan.<br /> <br /> Nice, I wonder if there was a plan what it could possibly have been. Perhaps gathering intelligence? Maybe he even swapped one of the students or staff with a changeling.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mnemon</span><br /> <br /> And now we have Mnemon herself! Who's childhood seems to be at once enchanted and unremarkable, although much of that is due to her POV as a centuries old exalt remembering back to her mortal years. Ragara and the Empress dominated her life then. Super cool though, her four greatest teachers when she was young were her mother, duh, and three monks, one of whom never spoke and wore a full head hood tied around his neck with a cord of orichalcum.<br /> <br /> She exalts while fighting him too, in a sparring match. After her exaltation she beats him mercilessly and we find out that, in fact, he wasn't just a monk, but a chosen of Secrets. I bet that was an embarassing day back in Heaven, having to explain getting thrashed by a day one exalted Dragonblood. I like the assassination attempt that Ragara tries on her though, poisoned barbs on the inside of a suit of tailor made armour.<br /> <br /> I think it's cool that she's so old too that she doesn't get sent to the Heptagram, but to Versino. Also I like that they have at least 20 monks on hand to deal with things if they go pear shaped. If a demon gets out nobody really kills it quite so good as a monk. Not good enough for whatever horrible second circle demon her instructor summoned though. It somehow tore through all seven immaculates and proceeded to fight the entire rest of the school. No wonder the Heptagram was constructed for crisis control. All die except one monk, who on the verge of victory gets killed by Mnemon so she can take the Thurible for herself.<br /> <br /> God damn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There were some really interesting intense stories in that chapter, here's hoping things get a little better for the POV characters in the next one, but I have my doubts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T01:27:40-08:00","id":1357174,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">A Life of Obligations</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cynis Takgana</span><br /> <br /> Well they get a little better as we see he becomes an itinerant monk, which we are told end up being essentially Immaculate Spec-ops monks. Wandering the world, reporting directly to the Mouth of Peace, and ferreting out the corrupt. She likes Takgana because he's more loyal to the Order than his house.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that's the end of the good news. He runs into his former betrothed, and all his old feelings of lust and love come rushing back, vowing right then to leave the order to be with her. Unfortunately, she's anathema, she fights him, breaks some of his ribs and then leaves, and he believes her to be dead, taken over by a demon. No breaks to be caught by Takgana apparently.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crow</span><br /> <br /> Oh come ON! After a stint in the legions she gets sent up against an army of fair folk without knowing that it's fairies she's fighting, so they're totally unequipped, she falls from a great height, as she always feared she would as a child, and then to top it all off her last desperate attempt at diplomacy with the being that killed her entire army lands her with her eyes plucked out. All because the lives of the slaves of paragon weren't hers to barter with, but instead it was her duty to protect them. It's awful, but then we actually get some really cool stuff. For one she's blind, but not always, because her awareness charms allow her to see through other's eyes. If someone is nearby that trusts her she can push her essence and allow her to see.<br /> <br /> The other cool thing is that, apparently, speaking the name of the Scarlett Empress is a bad idea, because it allows her sorcery to lock onto your location. At which point she unleashes the Sword of Creation on them and well that's pretty well that. That city that was saved though was Paragon. In 1e it looks like they became a satrapy because they faced annihilation to the Fair Folk and knew bending the knee to the Empress would be their only salvation. I think this is a departure in 2e, and I can't remember if 3e says anything.<br /> <br /> Still now she's planning on growing old and keeping a peaceful life. Well that doesn't really fit with the Empire falling apart, sadly. Well, at least she's become an expert in teaching blind fighting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ragara Jasir</span><br /> <br /> Yeah he's still gross. He's had a few personal religious experiences, but they've lead him to justify his practice of preying on people and manipulating them. Unlike Crow, who's constantly thinking, perhaps too much, about her own failures and how she could have done better, Jasir just forges forward, never even contemplating that he might have done something wrong. He's also murdered several people in the Thousand Scales and used his contacts there to benefit House Ragara over all others.<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to have him in my Dynastic game. I will enjoy my players meeting up with Kes and turning over his whole crooked operation.<br /> <br /> There's also one last section on family life where he says he regrets making up with his brother, but I don't wonder if there isn't a double meaning there, or even his own unconscious will. His brother raised a hand to him in jealousy, and soon after found himself in combat against rebels that slew him. It's possible that he just draws this incredibly sharp line where people who are family he's nice to, and everyone else is a tool for his ambition, but I find that somewhat out of character. I mean, yes, many people are like that to some degree, but they usually draw the line somewhere that includes their closest friends. Like if somebody is basically family, but not related by blood, they're still your people, but for Jasir they're just one or two mistakes away from being murdered.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moias</span><br /> <br /> Okay lets see what sickening fate befalls Moias later in life. Mhm, yep. She has a life of some adventure that seem to go okay, although her meeting with another fey for another mysterious set of minor interactions is probably building to something. After that though she returns to the isle and her entire sworn hearth gets executed, she just escapes the Imperial Force to flee to the city and be made a magistrate.<br /> <br /> Well at least she still has an old love to go back to, on rare occasion. This is just not nice in any way. They aren't even talking about the Realm disintegrating either, it's just their personal lives that suck.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mnemon</span><br /> <br /> Nearly right out of the gate Mnemon takes a husband, a sorcerer who teaches her things, and gets taught by her in return. He gives her three children and then, foolishly asking to marry her, earns his death. Apparently she knew one day she'd become Empress, and if he was still around that would be too much of a threat for her, so...yeah.<br /> <br /> Then we get an good look at House politics as she grows up. House Nellens being created as a huge disruption, of course. We also learn more about just how unwanted she is at the Heptagram. Even centuries later they're keeping the last survivor of Versino safely away.<br /> <br /> There's also a weird scene where Mnemon duels a Lunar anathema, killing him with poison and decapitating him...but then a flurry of dozens of other...Lunars? Show up? Like is a full quarter of the Silver Pact here? She also somehow gets away, leaving her companions to die. I can also see the complaint leveled against House Mnemon here that basically it was just an entire great house that was an extension of Mnemon herself. It kind of gives the impression that she has complete control over everything, along with insane trust issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know, even Machiavelli said in the Prince that it is best to be both loved and feared. The writing stylistically remains pretty solid, but I'm seeing a bit of creep from Air which had terrible things in it for sure, but it had a balance to it. Do any of these characters have any friends? Well ones who aren't executed in short order? Allies? Crow has one, but it looks like for everyone else the world is just out to kill them, and they're hateful, paranoid and hopeless. Jasir is a great villain but I'm really hoping Aspect Book: Fire gives some more NPCs that could go either way and aren't such wrecks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T02:18:48-08:00","id":1357176,"title":"","content":"There's a sense that the authors of Aspect Book Earth don't like the Realm very much and can't identify with these characters.<br /> <br /> This version of Mnemon doesn't appear to have earned a Great House but was given one by her mother, considering this is her own words she doesn't talk about any achievement and had the authority to have the father of her children executed on a whim then there couldn't have been much of a House Mnemon to speak of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T06:56:46-08:00","id":1357192,"title":"","content":"I actually sympathized a lot with Mnemon in AB:E despite all the horrible shit she does, its made very clear that she's a product of her environment instead of a bad seed from the beginning. It doesn't excuse her behavior, but I can see how she got there. I liked Takgana and Crow too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T08:35:43-08:00","id":1357202,"title":"","content":"I think part of the reason for the samey backstories in Aspect Book: Earth was rooted in their Aspect Abilities. Sorta like how every Earth Aspect got Martial Arts in 1e, so most of them learned to fight. Because every Earth Aspect got Resistance and Endurance, they often learn to endure pain and suffering (but, of course, that means there has to be pain and suffering to learn to resist).<br /> <br /> This was before 3e, where Dragon-Blooded pick from a list of Abilities within the purview of their Aspect. This was back when using Charms from outside your Aspect gave you a surcharge; just for optimization reasons, you wanted to use as many in-aspect powers as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T10:05:56-08:00","id":1357214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357176#post1357176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a sense that the authors of Aspect Book Earth don't like the Realm very much and can't identify with these characters.<br /> <br /> This version of Mnemon doesn't appear to have earned a Great House but was given one by her mother, considering this is her own words she doesn't talk about any achievement and had the authority to have the father of her children executed on a whim then there couldn't have been much of a House Mnemon to speak of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that also really stuck out. Mnemon casually murders mortal slaves to keep secrets for for necromancy, that\u2019s horrible but whatever she\u2019s an ancient exalt who\u2019s been raised to be a pretty heartless aristocrat. Her husband though? Wasn\u2019t he at least kind of politically powerful? When King James II had a bunch of his close associates murdered on a whim he then had to dole out a huge amount of land to the local lords to appease them and prevent a revolt. <br /> <br /> You could also have somebody try to actually actively move against her and she has them flayed or something. It\u2019s cruel, but she had a reason at least. I\u2019d lose a lot of sympathy for somebody getting executed if I knew they tried to kill my mother. On the other hand if I thought the head of my house was whimsically murdering even her most close and trusted allies, and nobody was safe, that\u2019s not a GOOD kind of fear for rulership. You don\u2019t want your subjects to be afraid they\u2019ll find a dagger in their throat because you were having a bad day and no other reason, you want your subjects to feel safe and protected by you and fear only rebelling against your rule. Jasir gets away with it because he\u2019s just a parasite that\u2019s wormed his way into the empire, and one who makes it very difficult to follow his actions. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to complain too much, like I said the writing is still very effective. Jasir is just such filth it\u2019s great. It would just be nice if there were some people like Kes or Meladus who aren\u2019t constantly depicted as being sickeningly cruel, and who are also working hard to change the society they love in for the better. Even if that \u201cfor the better\u201d ends up not being that great for non-imperials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T11:01:48-08:00","id":1357219,"title":"","content":"Exalted writing has historically had a problem with showing consequences for abuse of power besides the wish fufillment &quot;someone Exalts and kicks their ass&quot;.<br /> Probably the best example of this is when the Empress had most of the Deliberative slaughtered for not voting how she wanted and we're just told that their successors were more cooperative. At the very least a purge like that would make people with political aspirations avoid the Empress' attention and lead to a brain drain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T11:54:15-08:00","id":1357225,"title":"","content":"Yeah that always took me for a bit of a ride too, especially with the way the deliberative works. They\u2019re representatives of the powerful great houses, that kind of move would lead to a groundswell of disobedience at the very least, and more than a few open revolts. <br /> <br /> Also, and I know they\u2019re bureaucrats, but the deliberative had like over a hundred dynastic Dragonblooded right? Dynasts are brought up in a warrior culture where all of them are expected to be able to socialize as well as fight. What kind of massacre took place when they pulled that stunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T13:35:29-08:00","id":1357248,"title":"","content":"Looking back on it this depiction of Mnemon is kind of colouring the intro fiction too. Rather than being no-nonsense and to the point she's kinda petulant. She's all &quot;bluh bluh dirty anathema.&quot; and then gets kind of cowed into proper discourse by the overwhelming presence of the Mask of Winters. <br /> <br /> That and Ragara seeming to have perpetually sloppy and bungled assassination attempts in spite of being one of the most powerful people in the world. The whole thing puts to my mind a bunch of lizards clutching their hordes and hissing and snapping at eachother. That is, I imagine, the intent of the writing, but its serving to make Ragara and Mnemon, who are each the head of a family so large that they're more powerful than most nations, seem petty and small minded. <br /> <br /> One of the things I like a lot about the aspects is the philosophy attached to them, the idealism of Air, passions of Fire, and how the world is viewed through those lenses. I was looking forward to seeing Earth as the architects of stability and order, I'm just not seeing hardly any of it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T20:26:06-08:00","id":1357446,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">The World We Rule</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cynis Takgana</span><br /> <br /> We start off a bit more promising here, with Takgana talking about the Immaculate order and his belief in it. It's not much but at least it's positive. It's also short lived, as we go right into talking about how old and callous people are, uncaring and cruel. Then we find out that his mother has been telling everyone that he died, and in hearing that he shattered a wall and resigned to having a talk with his mother. Then Takgana talks about how he's envious of mortals for their blessedly short lives and lack of responsibility.<br /> <br /> He's also not attached to a house and very glad to be.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crow</span><br /> <br /> She is also showing a bit more affinity for the structures that surround her. For one she's funneling money back to her mortal parents, who now run the orchard in luxury. I like her one interaction with a Solar though. Sitting by the fireside, blind, unable to tell who she was talking to, they share a moment and depart, fleeing her companion. Her interactions with fairfolk are understandably, less pleasant. She's still after blood for them. I like how her exaltation has given her immediate family some dreams now though, wondering if the blood will manifest again.<br /> <br /> She's not attached to a house, very glad to be. Her relationship with mortals is complex though, she envies the Dynasts, who don't have so many mortal family members and won't have to watch so many die, but she also pities the mortals and admires how they're at peace with how replaceable they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ragara Jasir</span><br /> <br /> He's got a unique view of the Realm. He's basically 100% certain it will fall, but he's likewise certain something else will rise from the ashes. It's nice to see at least one of the characters with a bigger view and ambitions. His dark but completely valid interpretation of the Immaculate Faith also shows in his treatment of mortals. He tries to treat them well as the texts say, and even lobbies for their financial burdens to be eased compared to the other great houses, but as a ploy to keep their loyalty while uprisings overturn his rival's holdings.<br /> <br /> He's pretty blase about Anathema as well. Not because he doesn't realize there's a threat there, he just thinks that they're inconsequential compared to a united Realm, reasoning they were beaten before.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moias</span><br /> <br /> I'm liking Moias more as the book goes on. She's doing a lot more of what I expected from an Earth aspect. She's involving herself in the institutions of the Realm and working to cut away the corruption. She also seems to have a lot more true respect for mortals, even if it's because the peasants life is so much simpler than that of the Dynasty. I can see it refreshing for magistrates to live with mortal Archons who have way less interest in corrupting her to their own grand schemes.<br /> <br /> There's also a fittingly terrible story about them happening upon a young Solar who doesn't even really know what he is and killing him. I like how she justifies it in her faith too. The boy wanted to save his father who was buried under rubble, and she surmises that the anathema spirit must have taken hold of the poor lad in his moment of weakness. Her religous views on fair folk are actually pretty cool too. Believing them to have a similar reincarnation cycle that eventually leads them to nobility and eventually to being jadeborn.<br /> <br /> We also see that she's building a force of magistrates, known to eachother and governing themselves. Much more open and coordinated than the failing All-Seeing-Eye, which she hates and suspects will collapse soon.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mnemon</span><br /> <br /> Well we get a bit of her scheming for the throne and also...executing Tepet Ejava? Really? Weird I didn't think that was confirmed. She's also taking a running tally of all of the ills that the empire suffers, that's a good thing. She's also trying to use the Immaculate Order as a pillar to hold up the whole Realm, noting, probably correctly, that if the peasantry lose faith in the Dragonblooded that their infighting won't matter as the foundation will fall apart.<br /> <br /> Her view of her house is very top-down though. Everyone exists to serve her, and she also doesn't trust them, as she says the Empress wasn't right to trust her. They're all too ambitious, although from her characterization she'd be disappointed with them if they weren't. She's got an awesomely utilitarian view of mortals though, to her they're basically what yeast is to a baker. She's got a pretty complex view with the rest of the Immaculate Order though.<br /> <br /> Weirdly she's also using fair folk to protect her satrapies as she withdraws her armies. Offering them a percentage of the population in exchange for protection. That's not going to be sustainable, for sure, and it's just begging for a group of Solars to come upend it. At the end when she talks about the first age she has a really surprising lack of knowledge about the Shogunate. Like, I get it a lot of the records were lost, but most of the Blessed Isle was untouched, did she not know if the Shogun had a bunch of great houses?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think I liked this chapter a bit better, but I have higher hopes for Voices not our Own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T22:02:21-08:00","id":1357457,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Voices Not Our Own</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mortals</span><br /> <br /> Not much to say about the very first story except a mortal frightened of Takgana's power and anger.<br /> <br /> The next two stories though are about Jasir and his artful manipulation of people through assassination and economic pressure. The mortals, patrician and peasant, are being toyed with like pawns. These poor guys need somebody from the imperial treasury to take a closer look at Jasir, stat.<br /> <br /> I like the next story too, a guy who's wife paid off a judge to have him executed in an interesting way. Apparently in rural Juche a common execution is to be buried up to your neck in stones, and if anyone feels strongly enough about you to set you free they can work to dig you out. Moias though happened upon that scene in the third day, ferreted out the corruption in the judge and freed him, making him an archon. A dirty lowlife archon who fears her as much he's grateful, but useful nonetheless. Nothing like Tepet Elana has with her mortal friend and archon. Then a followup about another judge trying to leverage his family connections to wiggle out of Moias next investigation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dragonblooded</span><br /> <br /> We learn hear from a testimony of another teacher at the Stair that Crow's classes are going well. A blind woman teaching the sighted how to fight without eyes is pretty empowering. Keeping with the Stairs brutal nature though anyone dumb enough to try to ambush her outside of class gets one of their eyes taken. It's harsh, but with the rest of the way the Stair has been depicted in this book it's probably better to be humbled like that than actually killed.<br /> <br /> Crow's husband also confesses to something else. Silent Betrayer indeed, he had sex with their outcaste friend, now a monk. Rightly pointing out a monks vows of chastity and his wifes streak for vengeance an act that could cost both of them their lives, not to mention the horrible guilt afterwards. I don't wonder if this wasn't some plan orchestrated by another faction to keep control over Betrayer.<br /> <br /> Then a creepy testimonial from an outcaste who's fire aspected and clearly in Jasir's employ. You get a good sense here of just how wealthy he is and how he uses it. He personally pays for this outcaste to sit in a well furnished apartment and do only the occasional job for him. Just to have a relatively loyal personal wizard to tap into when he wants to. He's like a kraken, with his tentacles spread through and wrapping around everything.<br /> <br /> Oh Tepet Elana, how I've missed you! Suspicious of unifying the magistracy into a single organization, but understanding that some things must change, definitely a good mixing of counter philosophies.<br /> <br /> Mnemon's child also talks about how she respects her mother for putting her in the Immaculate Order, knowing she'd be a threat to her. Very consistent with Mnemon's impossible worldview, wanting to surround herself with capable people but fearing more than anything them usurping her, as she plans to take the throne. I don't know if she's ever considered that anyone in their life has ever just been loyal out of a sense of duty or love.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirits</span><br /> <br /> At last we get the culmination of this fey interaction. A fairie is now going to be hunting Moias for her love and spirit. Is it really possible that they could range so far into the center of the blessed isle? Or maybe there's some kind of plot brewing to draw her out, or near a spot where the Wyld can be accessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I definitely liked this chapter a lot better. Most of the characters in it just seems a lot more well balanced, although Mnemon's house is still portrayed as a weird scaffolding of mixed loyalties and backbiting. Next is Records From Before, and almost finished with Aspect Book Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T22:31:00-08:00","id":1357460,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Records of the Before</span><br /> <br /> Good old bit of post-apocalyptic warning signs, gotta love that.<br /> <br /> Then we move on to a letter from one of the Sidereal developers of the immaculate martial arts. She's arrogant and somewhat unwilling to hear wisdom from her younger Dragonblooded masters, but she also mentions re-designing the immaculate styles, implying that they've gone through some revisions early on.<br /> <br /> A bit after that there's a battle report from a Shogunate era fight against the fey with some stuff that's probably not kosher for 3e. For one in the fight there's three warstriders and three TALONS of Dragonblooded wearing Dragon Armor. That's almost 400 exalts in runic power armor, god damn. It's even implied that their mortal forces were wearing gunzosha and ashigaru armor as well. It looks like they might have been fighting the advance force of the huge wyld invasion mentioned in Air.<br /> <br /> Then there's actually a pretty cool letter from what appears to be a government agent fighting a rebellion, but whoever he is he takes a wide view of it. Understanding that there's a bunch of corruption going on back and forth here, and that even if they killed the revolutionaries because the base problem isn't going away and the prime actors are untouchable it's not really going to do anything.<br /> <br /> Yeah, looks like it was the same one Kejak is talking about the terrible losses incurred. Good logistics on it though, the airship docks being filled with chaos means that the military response arriving by air can't get to the ground. It also looks like he's referencing the shrinking of Creation from it's maximum first age size. That probably explains why much of the records form before have so much wyld fighting in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T22:58:22-08:00","id":1357461,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Miracles of Pasaip</span><br /> <br /> Not much to say here except the genesis of Skin Mount Amulets and Perfected Kata Bracers, both staples of 2e powergaming.<br /> <br /> Signature Characters<br /> <br /> Holy shit Takgana has a 5 in Martial Arts, Dodge, AND Dexterity, and 4 in Strength and Stamina. I did not really get the sense from his story that he was one of the most powerful martial artists out there but, yeah okay sure.<br /> <br /> Also I fucking knew Jasir killed his brother.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Other Notable Earth Aspects</span><br /> <br /> Immanent Thunder, one of the most powerful monks in the world. Aided by an enormous amount of Sidereal astrology, as well as harsh and incredibly expansive training he's become known for killing anathema in single combat with just his hands. It's kind of cool the idea that his destiny has been manipulated so hard for so long that it might be having strange affects on him and those around him. Much better to put that here than the old Mouth of Peace, who was basically just a will-less puppet for the Bronze Faction.<br /> <br /> OOOHH I like Dutiful Sparrow, an outcaste who was given a third choice, not the coin or the razor, but the green cloak of the Heptagram. She then became a teacher and the student death toll plummeted due to her demon knowledge. I'm not sure if having second and third circle demons take notice of her is necessary though. Like third circles? I dunno.<br /> <br /> Cynis Janisim, Takgana's mother, is interesting as well. She has more of a 3e feel to her house, where she rejects the debauchery and instead just attempts to make the greatest wines. Apparently she also destroyed and rebuilt the storehouse in a single night when she heard of her son's 'death'.<br /> <br /> Another cool plot hook with Ledaal Chiska mistaking Pasaip for Autocthon, the Great Maker in ancient texts. A manse builder who's secretly funneling power to the slumbering primordial and may form some kind of connection to it is pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Lastly Ragara Myrrun, one of three living Immaculate Grandmasters. Here we have no sidebar stating that Myrrun can not innitiate into Sidereal Martial Arts, merely that if he does so he will be changed in totally unpredictable ways. Here his depiction is a lot more mysterious that it was in Scroll of Exalts I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> AND that's it for Aspect Book: Earth! Overall I didn't like it as much as Air, but I think it finished very strong. It's just a bit too cynical and depressing for me. Next up is Fire!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T00:48:03-08:00","id":1357477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357446#post1357446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly she's also using fair folk to protect her satrapies as she withdraws her armies. Offering them a percentage of the population in exchange for protection. That's not going to be sustainable, for sure, and it's just begging for a group of Solars to come upend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my other big problem with her portrayal here. She's teamed up with Mask of Winters and is trying to use the Fair Folk, both of which feel like the actions of other more desperate contenders for the Scarlet Throne who can't summon second circle demons but with all of this on Mnemon it's just telling you she'd make a terrible Empress over and over again.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T00:54:05-08:00","id":1357479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357477#post1357477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my other big problem with her portrayal here. She's teamed up with Mask of Winters and is trying to use the Fair Folk, both of which feel like the actions of other more desperate contenders for the Scarlet Throne who can't summon second circle demons but with all of this on Mnemon it's just telling you she'd make a terrible Empress over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, her character just seems kind of small and not very with it or stable, when she should be one of the oldest characters with the biggest personalities, and an earth aspect to boot. She doesn't act like she has the stability or confidence that someon in her position should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:05:19-08:00","id":1357765,"title":"","content":"The aspect and caste books are some of my favorite exalted books. But it always seemed to me a great failure that none of the main characters in the Caste books came from Lookshy, it seems to me that they missed a great opportunity by not doing so.<br /> The closest thing is Karal Fire Orchid in Caste book Zenith.<br /> <br /> I will continue reading these summaries with great interest, it is always good to refresh the memory and it is quite interesting to see what others think of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:53:48-08:00","id":1357772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357765#post1357765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aspect and caste books are some of my favorite exalted books. But it always seemed to me a great failure that none of the main characters in the Caste books came from Lookshy, it seems to me that they missed a great opportunity by not doing so.<br /> The closest thing is Karal Fire Orchid in Caste book Zenith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does she <i>not</i> come from Lookshy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T09:59:05-08:00","id":1357809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357772#post1357772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does she <i>not</i> come from Lookshy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point was she's not in an Aspect book, being rather more of the shiny persuasion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:02:46-08:00","id":1357812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357809#post1357809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point was she's not in an Aspect book, being rather more of the shiny persuasion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, yeah, I get that, but they brought up the Caste books - twice, even - before making this statement about a lack of Lookshy characters. I actually <i>agree </i>that it's a failing of the Aspect books that we don't get any, say, Lookshyan Wood Aspects or Air Aspect Forest Witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:38:07-08:00","id":1357857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357812#post1357812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, yeah, I get that, but they brought up the Caste books - twice, even - before making this statement about a lack of Lookshy characters. I actually <i>agree </i>that it's a failing of the Aspect books that we don't get any, say, Lookshyan Wood Aspects or Air Aspect Forest Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* Dagurasu's statement fits as just about the Aspect books if you figure that second Caste or Aspect was supposed to be just Aspect. Or maybe Dagu feels Fire Orchid wasn't that Lookshyan? I could see an argument for that - as a character, she's not exactly enmeshed in the affairs or culture of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:54:11-08:00","id":1357865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357812#post1357812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, yeah, I get that, but they brought up the Caste books - twice, even - before making this statement about a lack of Lookshy characters. I actually <i>agree </i>that it's a failing of the Aspect books that we don't get any, say, Lookshyan Wood Aspects or Air Aspect Forest Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit late and too short, but one of the briefly-described characters of the Woodbook is a Lookshy intelligence asset who married into the Dynasty as a seemingly ordinary outcaste (&quot;seemingly&quot; because her uncle is in Seventh Legion Intelligence). Wood also has an independent outcaste who gets a full treatment in the book (Rutanjali). It would have been really nice to see that happen from the first book, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-30-2019, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:56:55-08:00","id":1357866,"title":"","content":"I gotta admit, aside from resolving a House's finances in the time it takes to eat a peach, and accidentally exploding one's sex partner with one's tantric techniques, a lot of Aspect Book: Wood didn't stick all that well in my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:32:55-08:00","id":1357878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357866#post1357866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta admit, aside from resolving a House's finances in the time it takes to eat a peach, and accidentally exploding one's sex partner with one's tantric techniques, a lot of Aspect Book: Wood didn't stick all that well in my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was the only AB I got, because its &quot;Records of the Past&quot; section has a reference to cell biology. An entirely predictable purchase on my part. Also, it had a Lunar grand grimcleaver, and introduced the stats for said giant axes into the game for the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:47:14-08:00","id":1357879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357866#post1357866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta admit, aside from resolving a House's finances in the time it takes to eat a peach, and accidentally exploding one's sex partner with one's tantric techniques, a lot of Aspect Book: Wood didn't stick all that well in my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uuuugh. <i>Bhagwei</i>. Wish I could get him and his idiotic incestuous backstory <i>out</i> of my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could maybe take it from a more clearly villainous figure, but the book....<br /> <br /> Apologies to Doc, this is a pet hate. Just.... setting up to rant about him fully once Doc reaches Wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:52:31-08:00","id":1357881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357879#post1357879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wish I could get him and his idiotic incestuous backstory <i>out</i> of my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could maybe take it from a more clearly villainous figure...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, can you clarify this statement? Maybe I'm just confused (been having to follow a lot of discussions today), but it read to me like you want him to be evil, because he's the product of incest. Do I have that right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T14:16:40-08:00","id":1357884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1357881#post1357881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, can you clarify this statement? Maybe I'm just confused (been having to follow a lot of discussions today), but it read to me like you want him to be evil, because he's the product of incest. Do I have that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* You asked Count! :P Spoilering so Doc can go into this relatively unprejudiced<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">'Think he should be evil because he's the product of incest' Oh, no. I find him to be <i>thoroughly </i>evil because he initiated a sexual relationship with a student, (a dynamic with an inherent power imbalance) incorporated dangerous practices to that relationship, <b>got her killed through those practices</b> and sees nothing wrong with any of that. I would be somewhat willing to overlook that if the book presented him as more of a bleak antagonistic figure, in a similar light to Deled or Lahor, but instead.... sidebar on doing your own wacky tantric charm experiments! Setting him up as the guy investigating Deathknights, trying to cure the Great Contagion! Would make a great Emperor but is too dedicated to his art!<br /> <br /> The incest thing is really just <i>added </i>stupid. As is skinning a small girl and wearing her as a cloak. As is the Empress killing a lover she just had saved from death. Bhagwei's story is like a stupid magnet - other bits of Wood are also <i>very </i>stupid, like Ejava Sexing Information out of Pirate Captain Through Sex, but Bhagwei is the one that gets me legitimately furious. It's like Deathstroke and Tara Markov - that stuff's just not okay, and acting like he's just another Dynast infuriates me.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T15:59:02-08:00","id":1357892,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T07:49:54-08:00","id":1358003,"title":"","content":"TBH, I consider that particular....&quot;origin story&quot; to be more informative of how screwed up Ragara and Cynis were rather than of Bhagwei himself(which makes me wonder why AB:E didn't include Ragara in the &quot;Other Exalts&quot; section if they really wanted to drive it home)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T09:24:25-08:00","id":1358022,"title":"","content":"I actually don't think you can read Bhagwei's description of events, taking him at face value, and come to that interpretation... But! This is unreliable narrators for you. Not going to distract from the Doctor's thread by going down this tangent before he hits Wood tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T09:51:38-08:00","id":1358026,"title":"","content":"I get how Bhagwei's thing could upset someone in a way it wasn't intended to.<br /> It's the single biggest problem with the Aspect Books, spending so much time with these characters means that sometimes the way those little anecdotes are employed is pretty thoughtless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T00:57:00-08:00","id":1358155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358026#post1358026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get how Bhagwei's thing could upset someone in a way it wasn't intended to.<br /> It's the single biggest problem with the Aspect Books, spending so much time with these characters means that sometimes the way those little anecdotes are employed is pretty thoughtless.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the problem, I figure I'd have that reaction to bits in the other Aspect books, right? Like, I've read all five aspect, all five caste, <i>none </i>get to me quite like Bhagwei. There's little bits of writing I'd roll my eyes at, but nothing close to the anger, and honestly even eye rolls were rare outside Wood. I think 'Elana's assistant has a crush on her, because of course he does' but that hardly angered me. I just found it lazy writing. Other characters did morally repugnant things - Mnemon murders innocents at least twice, and while one of those I found stupid, it didn't elicit this kinda hate.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">*shrug* Maybe it's RW bias on my part - abuse of authority and power like that is something I find quite upsetting. But I feel weird that I'm the only one in the fandom that I've ever encountered who has this visceral a reaction to the guy. It might not be en par with some of the grotesque stuff that happened later, but it's thoroughly abhorrent. It even low key slut shames the victim - taking care to note Bhagwei selected her because of her boasting about her performance in the bedroom. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T01:37:39-08:00","id":1358158,"title":"","content":"Bhagwei is my favourite Dynast.<br /> <br /> Heroic ambition. Abuse of power. Family politics not quite walked away from. Hits all my good notes.<br /> <br /> The Dynasts aren't good people.<br /> <br /> And tropes become tropes because they usually follow a logical consequence. I don't think it's lazy writing to call on them.<br /> <br /> I can see the point Croakamancer (whom I believe takes their handle from a someone who abuses her power to rape and torture a prisoner of war in her care) is making. Bhagwei is a squicky rapist who no doubt sets off triggers. But he's an elemental super-solider/fantasy kingdom prince/headmaster of a magic school: I don't think the presentation of his character/background requires any additional suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> I, personally, find him evocative and entertaining. Other people are going to find him stupid and insensitive. I respect your opinion, but I respectfully disagree. (There's an older thread discussing Bhagwei if there's interest in debate: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...goddamned-game</a> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T02:49:48-08:00","id":1358164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358158#post1358158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> can see the point Croakamancer (whom I believe takes their handle from a someone who abuses her power to rape and torture a prisoner of war in her care)</div> </div> </div> </div>... John, you don't come across like you're interested in <i>debate </i>or like you respect my opinion when you start taking shots like that.<br /> <br /> For the record, I use this tag because, in isolation, I find it a funny alternate name for necromancy. I'm not a fan of Wanda, or the comic as a whole for that matter. That's just a term I like that stuck with me.<br /> <br /> Your points, as far as I can tell, don't remotely track with any of my complaints. But eh. Let's adjourn to that other thread. You've already necromancied it, I feel like cutting loose 100%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T03:41:10-08:00","id":1358169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358155#post1358155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was the problem, I figure I'd have that reaction to bits in the other Aspect books, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I know people who've reacted to different parts of these books. The Mnemon stuff almost derailed a game I was running because of how it'd gotten to one of my players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T03:46:51-08:00","id":1358171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358169#post1358169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. I know people who've reacted to different parts of these books. The Mnemon stuff almost derailed a game I was running because of how it'd gotten to one of my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Fair enough. I guess it's all in what strikes a chord with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T19:05:55-08:00","id":1358749,"title":"","content":"So my home internet has been down for a while, I've read most of Fire, so I'll just skim it again as I write.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Aspect Book: Fire</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Intro Fiction</span><br /> <br /> So we start off with who we will come to know as Nellends Malakai, who's arriving to the Neck aboard the Dancing Ration. A ship that was supposed to be carrying three Dragonblooded and with much fanfare. Instead what happened is they were attacked by an Abyssal pirate at sea, who slew two of them and then was killed by Malakai, the youngest and now only exalted survivor. Interesting that Malakai recognizes the island's badge of office and is willing to bet a talent of jade that it's somehow enchanted. We often don't see a lot of magical stuff that can be used by non-exalts.<br /> <br /> I'm also surprised that in spite of the local leader being incredibly humble before the Dynast that Malakai is willing to admit failure on behalf of the Realm in keeping the waters safe from Abyssals. Although he quickly twists and turns it as to threaten to take his wives and children hostage on the Blessed Isle now that the supposed threat is gone. Diplomatically, quite adeptly, the chief just offers to pay the tribute owed now instead of later.<br /> <br /> Then more bad news, an irresponsible and probably overzealous Immaculate Monk was through a few months ago and ordered them to put a stop to their religious practice appeasing the god of Hungry Waters, and then left without dealing with the angry god. Also maybe the first appearance of the Thousand Hungry Wings which is in the new Devil's Parade. Malakai saves the city from it in a bittersweet moment where he's basically fixing a bunch off problems that the Dynasty was supposed to have fixed already, except often too late.<br /> <br /> Depending on the nature of the sacrifices demanded by the God of Hungry Waters it might be a bungled blessing or a curse that monk came around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Introduction</span><br /> <br /> Here's some off the stuff that I like, the philosophy of fire. Passion and drive, but also a cultural call to harness that passion in a direction and have discipline. It's cool that in the Realm Fire is actually the element of self control, specifically because fire wants to burn out so easily. It's also nice to see different examples in the fiction section like Achilles and Thor as fire aspects, who'd normally not be considered DBs at all because of their powers.<br /> <br /> Also some good Storytelling advice in general asking about the tone of the game and what the characters are going to be like before it starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T04:42:04-08:00","id":1358832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358158#post1358158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the point Croakamancer (whom I believe takes their handle from a someone who abuses her power to rape and torture a prisoner of war in her care) is making.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Upon reflection this really doesn't sit right with me as a member of the forum's moderation team even if you did apologise for it. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T05:36:31-08:00","id":1359053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358749#post1358749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my home internet has been down for a while, I've read most of Fire, so I'll just skim it again as I write.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Aspect Book: Fire</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Intro Fiction</span><br /> <br /> Instead what happened is they were attacked by an Abyssal pirate at sea, who slew two of them and then was killed by Malakai, the youngest and now only exalted survivor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Introduction</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Three Dragon-Blooded managing to kill an Abyssal is a great success. Even if two Dragon-Blooded die in combat. A perfectly possible result in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T13:31:05-08:00","id":1359125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358749#post1358749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Introduction</span><br /> <br /> Here's some off the stuff that I like, the philosophy of fire. Passion and drive, but also a cultural call to harness that passion in a direction and have discipline. It's cool that in the Realm Fire is actually the element of self control, specifically because fire wants to burn out so easily. It's also nice to see different examples in the fiction section like Achilles and Thor as fire aspects, who'd normally not be considered DBs at all because of their powers.<br /> <br /> Also some good Storytelling advice in general asking about the tone of the game and what the characters are going to be like before it starts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also curiously close to the Daoist xing of Fire corresponding to propriety, at least when speaking about it in a yang sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T13:41:17-08:00","id":1359128,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall liking Malakai, although I'm sure I'm forgetting some of his flaws. At least it seemed like he genuinely felt bad for the terrible position that the chief had been left in by that idiot monk, and he put himself in the line of fire to deal with the problem.<br /> <br /> That doesn't exactly make him a nice guy, but at least he's trying to be responsible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T22:14:49-08:00","id":1359210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359053#post1359053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three Dragon-Blooded managing to kill an Abyssal is a great success. Even if two Dragon-Blooded die in combat. A perfectly possible result in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a pretty anticlimactic end to a celestial exalt, which doesn't happen much. A failed pirate attack against a Realm ship that wasn't like a specific trap to kill them or anything. They also weren't even the main focus of what the satrapy's problem was. It's kind of weird because in other editions the presence of even a single Abyssal would bend the whole narrative around them to be the main villain and put to shame the petty concerns of the island god. Instead they're just kind of another danger lurking out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359128#post1359128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't exactly make him a nice guy, but at least he's trying to be responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and I don't know if NPCs really should be perfectly clean moral heroes anyway. For one there's always going to be a lot of games where they're antagonists, so you don't really want to be like &quot;Well now sadly you gotta kill Dynast Superman. Just don't try to think about poor sweet Ma and Pa Kent mourning the loss of their perfect son.&quot; It also leaves some room for the players to be that if they want. Or just open the door to saying &quot;Hey, this is the brutal world you live in, you can actually play the game of thrones and not feel too bad about not always being the best guy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either way I think I like the PoV characters from Fire a lot more than Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T23:27:07-08:00","id":1359214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359210#post1359210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly a pretty anticlimactic end to a celestial exalt, which doesn't happen much. A failed pirate attack against a Realm ship that wasn't like a specific trap to kill them or anything. They also weren't even the main focus of what the satrapy's problem was. It's kind of weird because in other edition<b>s</b> the presence of even a single Abyssal would bend the whole narrative around them to be the main villain and put to shame the petty concerns of the island god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>Second</i> Edition anyway. Third Edition has yet to mandate to me what my characters should and shouldn't consider threatening.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T21:12:36-08:00","id":1359839,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:22px\">Childhood and Self</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Peleps Danic Damanchina</span><br /> <br /> Interesting to see a fire aspected bureaucrat! It looks like they're setting her up to be maybe a bit of a criminal like Jasir but she seems less icky. Only a bit though, she's still growing up taking advantage of people. She also treats a lot of stuff like a game, which might contribute to her zero-sum outlook on life. Any time somebody else wins you must have lost. She also shows the insane pressure the children are under though, this really has the feeling of being wrought in fire. If she hadn't exalted she would have killed herself for her failure.<br /> <br /> There's also a description of the absolute perfection you feel just as you exalt, and some people going crazy trying to recreate it again. Her experience at the Spiral Academy is kind of cold and full of hard work, but she has a kind of sentimentality about it over the bonds she formed. Also a focus on training the actual ability of the students absent charms. I would think it because charms are based on mundane ability but they don't really imply that here. Also good reference to how many people in espionage and the FBI are actually accountants hunting down/commuting white collar crime.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nellens Malakai</span><br /> <br /> The sorcerer from the intro fiction! Apparently his parents were very open about sex and I guess free spirited. Also just like Damanchina Malakai was a bit of a prodigy from early on, and resents the people who can't keep up. He also brings up the idea of the Realm killing children who don't seem promising so that they don't add weakness into the Dragonblooded host.I can see it being a thing that has happened before 100%, but not a matter of policy. Especially for making one mistake in their second year of primary school, that's bordering on grimderp.<br /> <br /> Humiliation in front of classmates that you have mutual resentment for? That's more than plausible though. He also becomes completely determined to become a sorcerer, in spite of being from house Nellens, and thus having more obstacles put in his way on that road. There's also a pretty cool description of the Heptagram and how magical it is. The waters around it are filled with bound elementals and the grounds surrounding the huge buildings are prowling with demons.<br /> <br /> We also get some of his philosophy about risk and knowledge, one that we know will take him far away from the center of the Empire. Also apparently martial arts training and weapons training are staples at the Heptagram, which makes more sense in a game where Dynast chargen has bonus ability dots and trait minimums. True to university they don't actually do much interesting stuff until later years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cynis Denovah Avaku</span><br /> <br /> <br /> So right off the bat he grew up an impoverished noble and will grow to be fairly devout. Although he still attended one of the best primary schools because his parents put more money than they could afford into his education. We also know that it paid off because his children attend the best schools in the Realm and he has ambitions to make his family line large and powerful, renewing the old glory it once had. His exaltation though catapults him way ahead, and I like that they're focusing a lot more on the instant social power that it comes with rather than the magic.<br /> <br /> Apparently it's not enough to guarantee admission to the House of Bells though, which is a bit weird? Aren't there like, only 4 real secondary schools in the Realm, they all seem pretty hard to get into except for the Cloister of Wisdom. At least he's worried that all his really hard work and all the money put into it won't be enough. Then he seeks spiritual guidance to sooth his fears, but all he gets for it is a monk beating his head around and telling him, probably rightly, that if you've made every effort to succeed you shouldn't dwell on worrying about failing, even if you do you just need to find a way to push forward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sesus Rafara</span><br /> <br /> Rafara starts off with a pretty cheery childhood. Not uncommonly for Dynasts being a lot more attached to and affectionate with her nannies than parents. She's also not attending school but instead taking home tutors. For a Dynast that cost shouldn't mean too much, but it's going to isolate her, making her perfect to be an impartial spy or assassin later in life. Another prodigy among her peers as well.<br /> <br /> I do remember her exaltation story as it is super brutal. her mother, resentful of her and her nannies, takes them on a cruise to feed them all to the sharks. Rafara sadly exalting too late to save either of them, only herself. It is the day she vows to kill her mother though, and I suspect her lifelong revenge motivation will be a key part of her story.<br /> <br /> She doesn't attend secondary school either, still being constructed by Sesus to be a weapon to wield against other families. As a spy primarily though, rather than an assassin, so she's expert at information gathering. An interesting take on her education too, to keep her as an outsider they hire tutors from all over Creation. I wonder if that means the satrapies or outside the Realm as well?<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cathak Cainen</span><br /> <br /> Sweet, Cathak Cainen is one of the PoVs. He always seemed to be a relatively straightforward honourable sort. Apparently House Cathak isn't kidding around with that either, getting their children to perform tasks that other houses have servants for. They clean their own laundry like a peasant. We also get a little hint of Cainen having more of a heart than some of the other characters, taking on responsibilities for his big sister so she can get some rest.<br /> <br /> There's some more good writing voice here too, like cheekily referring to his older brothers lies as &quot;Naijanese&quot;. His older brother is also a bastard and a sadist, who puts the hurt on Cainen on day and prompting his exaltation. After his exaltation he pays his brother back for every bad thing and totally messes up his face. Normally that might be healed by magic in the Realm, but his dad suspects Naijan of being the result of his wife having an affair, and recognizes his cruelty so it's stone cold denial, even to the point of telling the healers at school to let him heal on his own.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough even though his brother was really mean to him, Cainen feels a lot off guilt for hurting him so badly, forcing him to go through weeks of pain, and maybe costing him a marriage. That guilt drives him to learn at the Cloister instead of one of the fancy expensive schools. I like his philosophy about the structure of the order too. It's good, it gives purpose and allows for harmonious action, but it can also be bad, when people become blinded by their traditions and cease to think.<br /> <br /> Also teaching &quot;perseverance, integrity, self-esteem and courtesy&quot; is apparently part of the curriculum, which actually might be more valuable than some of the other institutions focus on academics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think I'm definitely liking Fire a lot. The characters are pretty unique and diverse, and with mostly appropriate levels of really intense and high pressure upbringings without taking it too far. Really looking forward to how they grow and evolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T00:04:58-08:00","id":1359852,"title":"","content":"How Cathak Cainan's father handled infidelity is super questionable in the context of the Realm, particularly the aside where he mentioned his mother almost died because of it.<br /> <br /> It seems to be a fault of the author as Cainan's reflections on the matter don't seem to acknowledge that this is unusual behaviour that would've only further embarassed the House if it had ran its course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T09:16:06-08:00","id":1359905,"title":"","content":"Yeah that was pretty weird. Also Cynis Avaku vowing to rebuild his family line, he\u2019s actually lucky he married a mortal or he\u2019d be out of luck in that department.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T14:13:19-08:00","id":1360200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359839#post1359839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Childhood and Self</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do remember her exaltation story as it is super brutal. her mother, resentful of her and her nannies, takes them on a cruise to feed them all to the sharks. Rafara sadly exalting too late to save either of them, only herself. It is the day she vows to kill her mother though, and I suspect her lifelong revenge motivation will be a key part of her story.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Rafara has a horrible mother. It is one of the parts of the book that I always remember perfectly. More than the brutality itself by the sheer pettiness that motivates the act itself.<br /> Rafara is also interesting because it shows that sometimes the existence of descendants of the Great Houses, especially exalted, is deliberately concealed to use them as agents whose connection to that house cannot be proven in any way. An interesting concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359852#post1359852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Cathak Cainan's father handled infidelity is super questionable in the context of the Realm, particularly the aside where he mentioned his mother almost died because of it.<br /> <br /> It seems to be a fault of the author as Cainan's reflections on the matter don't seem to acknowledge that this is unusual behaviour that would've only further embarassed the House if it had ran its course.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in the first edition, but even then Realm was matriarchal. It is strange, but perhaps if the wife was of a much lower social category or if the House to which the silence belonged the possible scandal could somehow make sense. Even so, it is strange and it is difficult to fit it with Realm as we know it.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1359839#post1359839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yeah that was pretty weird. Also Cynis Avaku vowing to rebuild his family line, he\u2019s actually lucky he married a mortal or he\u2019d be out of luck in that department.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If I remember correctly his wife is from House Mnemon, good lineage, so it is not a bad arrangement given his situation.<br /> I like Avaku as character, he has clear and reasonable ambitions and at the same time, with reasonable doubts about Realm and his society.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","user":"Dagurasu","date":". 01-10-2020, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T15:45:29-08:00","id":1360216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1360200#post1360200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was in the first edition, but even then Realm was matriarchal. It is strange, but perhaps if the wife was of a much lower social category or if the House to which the silence belonged the possible scandal could somehow make sense. Even so, it is strange and it is difficult to fit it with Realm as we know it.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not just a case of if he could get away with killing her. Any speculation that the Water Aspect isn't his son is going to be bolstered by his wife disappearing around the same time. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}